  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#356\", \"PowerToys#38791\", \"PowerToys#17147\"], \"answer\": \"The core of this request, showing folder sizes in the File Explorer Details view, has been reported many times. PowerToys#356 is the main tracking ticket, and PowerToys#17147 was closed as a duplicate of it. Other duplicates include #38791, #7260, #31718 and #14847. Please follow and upvote #356 rather than opening a new request. It's still a feature request, so nothing in PowerToys shows folder sizes in Explorer yet. In the meantime, PowerToys Peek shows a folder's size, and the tickets suggest third-party tools such as WinDirStat, WizTree, the Folder Size shell extension, or the Files app. The tickets don't cover your extra ideas of automatic size-based folder colors and per-folder color choices. A visual size view is closest to the treemap idea in PowerToys#11871, so you could add your color idea there.\"}",
